<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Sign in with Apple (M1.3). Entitlements are consumed only at codesign
	     time, so CI's `flutter build ios --no-codesign` is unaffected; the
	     emulator integration tests never invoke native ASAuthorization either.
	     App Attest (com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment) is
	     deliberately NOT declared yet - deferred to the on-device/Mac slice
	     with the rest of prod App Check attestation (docs/architecture.md). -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!-- com.apple.developer.associated-domains IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT (ADR-040).
	     It was here, claiming applinks:ikimiz.web.app and
	     applinks:ikimiz.beyondkaira.com (ADR-036/039), and it was REMOVED so a
	     build could ship. Read ADR-040 before adding it back — the reason is a
	     hard external dependency, not an oversight.

	     The entitlement must also exist in the PROVISIONING PROFILE, which means
	     the Associated Domains capability has to be enabled on the App ID in the
	     Apple Developer portal. `match` fetches profiles READONLY (ADR-032), so
	     it cannot add the capability itself: a build claiming a domain its
	     profile does not carry fails at CODESIGN with an entitlement mismatch.
	     Measured, not assumed — no build has ever been signed with this key
	     (build 110 came from fa990e6, which predates ADR-036), so the portal
	     capability has never been exercised and cannot be presumed present.

	     While it is absent, invite links still work — they just resolve in the
	     BROWSER rather than opening the app. https://ikimiz.web.app/i/<code>
	     serves a page showing the code with a copy button, and the invitee
	     enters it via "Have a code?" (PartnerPreviewScreen). That is one extra
	     step for the invitee and zero blocked releases, which is the trade
	     ADR-040 makes.

	     TO RESTORE (in this order, or the build breaks):
	       1. enable Associated Domains for com.beyondkaira.hayati in the
	          Apple Developer portal and let the profile regenerate;
	       2. re-add the key below with BOTH hosts;
	       3. the AASA is ALREADY served and correct at
	          https://ikimiz.web.app/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
	          (verified live) — Apple fetches it at INSTALL time over TLS and
	          follows no redirects, so nothing else is needed there.
	     Keep the host list mirroring kInviteLinkHosts in invite_deep_link.dart:
	     the app must not parse a host iOS was never told to hand it.

	     The custom `hayati://` scheme in Info.plist is untouched throughout, so
	     invites already sitting in someone's chat history keep working. -->
</dict>
</plist>
